          "message": "Validate Timestamp conversion from SystemTimes before UTC Epoch time\n\nThe protobuf spec for `Timestamp` states that:\n\n    negative second values with fractions must still have\n    non-negative nanos values that count forward in time\n\n... but in v0.6.1 and earlier of `prost_types`, this is handled wrongly\nwhen converting to `SystemTime`, with the `nanos` value contributing to\nthe `Duration` that is to be _subtracted_ from the `UNIX_EPOCH`:\nhttps://github.com/danburkert/prost/blob/v0.6.1/prost-types/src/lib.rs#L142-L145\n\n```Rust\nlet mut duration = Duration {\n    seconds: -timestamp.seconds,\n    nanos: timestamp.nanos,\n};\n```\n\nSo, for example `Timestamp { seconds: -20, nanos: 999_999_999 }` would\nresult in a `Duration { seconds: 20, nanos: 999_999_999 }` to subtract\nfrom `UNIX_EPOCH`, instead of the correct value of 19 seconds + 1 nano\nbefore `UNIX_EPOCH`.\n\nThe bug was fixed in commit 4ad5e3451fcd2e2192406351671a962e2e2be909\n(https://github.com/danburkert/prost/pull/297), which replaces the old\n`TryFrom` implementation with a full `From<Timestamp> for SystemTime`,\nand adds `From<SystemTime> for Timestamp` support for pre-UTC Epoch time\n`SystemTime` values.  However, the existing unittests do not include any\nspecific validation for timestamps earlier than the UTC epoch time.\n\nThis patch therefore adds a set of representative test cases which make\nsure that the protobuf spec is respected.  This should prevent the risk\nof regressions in future.  These are provided in two separate functions:\n\n  * `check_timestamp_negative_seconds` provides general purpose\n    checks, with nanos values provided in 100 ns increments so\n    as to guarantee the same behaviour on all platforms (POSIX\n    `SystemTime` has 1 ns resolution, but Windows only 100 ns)\n\n  * `check_timestamp_negative_seconds_1ns` provides tests that\n    include nanos values down to 1 ns resolution, which will\n    only work on POSIX systems\n\nPart of https://github.com/danburkert/prost/issues/327.",
